{
  "about": "What `complete` and `hover` answer, for the manifest in the package. The TypeScript core (core/scripts/check-core.ts) and Kotlin (EditingParityTest.kt) are both held to every case. `|` in `text` is the cursor and is not part of the text; positions are UTF-16 units. For `complete`, `expect` says: `count`, how many suggestions; `kinds`, the kinds among them; `range`, the `start` and `end` every one has; `labels`, every label in order; `first` and `last`, the labels at the ends; `has`, suggestions that are among them, compared on the fields written. For `hover`, `expect` is the answer, or null.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "every class inside a class attribute, and the word at the cursor is what is replaced",
      "call": "complete",
      "text": "<button class=\"lt-bu|t\"></button>",
      "html": true,
      "expect": {
        "count": 80,
        "kinds": ["class"],
        "range": {
          "start": 15,
          "end": 21
        },
        "first": "lt-accordion",
        "last": "lt-theme-control",
        "has": [
          {
            "label": "lt-divider",
            "kind": "class",
            "detail": "Divider",
            "documentation": "**Divider** · A line between parts of the content. A CSS component with one class and no JavaScript.\n\n`data-variant`: subtle, strong (default without the attribute)\n\n[Documentation](https://lo-tek.sobernetics.no/components/divider/)",
            "start": 15,
            "end": 21
          },
          {
            "label": "lt-button",
            "kind": "class",
            "detail": "Button",
            "start": 15,
            "end": 21
          },
          {
            "label": "lt-dialog__title",
            "kind": "class",
            "start": 15,
            "end": 21
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "the classes are the same outside HTML",
      "call": "complete",
